{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "James Taylor feels like a natural next choice because his acoustic songwriting matches what I enjoy about Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards.",
    "The Lovin' Spoonful fits my interest in Melanie and mid-sixties hits, while Eagles also connects with my enjoyment of familiar melodic rock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Journey feels too much like arena rock for my current mood; sharing a classic-rock connection does not give me the gentler folk-pop sound I want today.",
    "Simon and Garfunkel's Greatest Hits appeals musically, but I expect substantial overlap with the best-of collection I already interacted with, so I have little reason to choose it now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices lean too heavily on my interest in classic rock without distinguishing mellow songwriting from bigger, more forceful rock.",
    "My history of choosing greatest-hits collections seems to be treated as enough reason to offer another compilation, even when the songs may overlap with a collection I already explored."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards and Melanie matters because I am especially drawn to gentle melodies and folk-oriented songwriting right now.",
    "Liking an artist or collection does not always mean I would choose it today: Bread and Fleetwood Mac appeal, but James Taylor more closely fits my present mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older melodic hits, but give too little weight to my current preference for gentle folk-pop and avoiding overlapping collections."
}"}
